-( print Function Implementation )
-{
    Location: mc2/core/print.spacetime
    
    Features:
    - Variadic arguments via _possible_args_
    - Supports multiple types (int, float, str)
    - Hardware I/O via io_write syscall
    - Handles up to 8 arguments (registers %r0-%r7)
    
    Usage Example:
    @main:
        :: load.const << "Hello, " >> -> %r0
        :: load.const << "world" >> -> %r1
        :: load.const << "!" >> -> %r2
        :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r3  -(null terminator)
        :: call << @print >>
        :: return
    
    Implementation Details:
    - Uses %r10 as argument counter
    - Uses %r11 for comparison operations
    - Uses %r12 for null checking
    - Iterates through registers %r0-%r7
    - Stops when encountering null/zero value
    - Each argument is output via io_write syscall
}

-( input Function Implementation )
-{
    Location: mc2/core/input.spacetime
    
    Features:
    - Optional prompt parameter
